Subject: [PATCH] restartsig: restart dwm in place (SIGHUP) / clean exit (SIGTERM)

Ports dwm-restartsig-20180523-6.2.diff (dwm.suckless.org/patches/restartsig)
onto chadwm, adapted to chadwm names/style.

What it does:
  * `static int restart` flag.
  * quit() gains an arg: quit({.i = 1}) sets `restart` before stopping the
    loop; quit({.i = 0}) (or {0}) is the old plain quit.
  * SIGHUP  -> sighup()  -> quit({1})  (recompile then `pkill -HUP chadwm`,
    or bind a key, to reload the binary without logging out).
  * SIGTERM -> sigterm() -> quit({0})  (logout / `kill` shuts dwm down
    cleanly instead of it dying to the default SIGTERM disposition).
  * main() re-execs `execvp(argv[0], argv)` after cleanup() when `restart`.

Window placement across the restart is already preserved by chadwm's existing
_NET_CLIENT_INFO handling (setclienttagprop() + the read-back in manage()),
so the companion preserveonrestart patch is not needed. Per-tag mfact /
nmaster / layout are NOT persisted (same limitation as upstream).

Independent of docs/dwm-6.5-parity.patch - the two patches touch disjoint
lines and apply in either order.

Known limitation: glibc signal() installs handlers with SA_RESTART, so
XNextEvent() is not interrupted; a SIGHUP/SIGTERM is acted on at the next X
event rather than immediately. This matches the upstream patch and is not
addressed here (a self-pipe would be the fix).

Suggested config.h keybind (add yourself):
    { MODKEY|ShiftMask, XK_r, quit, {1} },   // restart in place
and, if you also want a plain quit:
    { MODKEY|ShiftMask, XK_q, quit, {0} },
The existing signals[] entry { "quit", quit } also means
`chadwm-msg quit i 1` (or your dwmc wrapper) restarts once wired up.

Apply from the repo root:  git apply docs/restartsig.patch
---
diff --git a/dwm.c b/dwm.c
index b515686..c153b9d 100644
--- a/dwm.c
+++ b/dwm.c
@@ -311,6 +311,8 @@ static void placemouse(const Arg *arg);
 static void pop(Client *client);
 static void propertynotify(XEvent *e);
 static void quit(const Arg *arg);
+static void sighup(int unused);
+static void sigterm(int unused);
 static Client *recttoclient(int x, int y, int w, int h);
 static Monitor *recttomon(int x, int y, int w, int h);
 static void removesystrayicon(Client *i);
@@ -430,6 +432,7 @@ static void (*event_handlers[LASTEvent])(XEvent *) = {
     [UnmapNotify] = unmapnotify};
 static Atom wm_atom[WMLast], net_atom[NetLast], xembed_atom[XLast];
 static int running = 1;
+static int restart = 0;
 static Cur *cursor[CurLast];
 static Clr **scheme, border_clr;
 static Display *display;
@@ -2932,8 +2935,24 @@ void propertynotify(XEvent *e) {
   }
 }
 
-/* stop the main event loop */
-void quit(const Arg *arg) { running = 0; }
+/* stop the main event loop; arg->i != 0 asks main() to re-exec dwm afterwards */
+void quit(const Arg *arg) {
+  if (arg->i)
+    restart = 1;
+  running = 0;
+}
+
+/* SIGHUP: restart dwm in place (re-exec after cleanup) */
+void sighup(int unused) {
+  Arg a = {.i = 1};
+  quit(&a);
+}
+
+/* SIGTERM: exit cleanly (e.g. on logout) instead of being killed */
+void sigterm(int unused) {
+  Arg a = {.i = 0};
+  quit(&a);
+}
 
 /* return the PID that owns an X window */
 pid_t winpid(Window w) {
@@ -3617,6 +3636,8 @@ void setup(void) {
                   LeaveWindowMask | StructureNotifyMask | PropertyChangeMask;
   XChangeWindowAttributes(display, root, CWEventMask | CWCursor, &wa);
   XSelectInput(display, root, wa.event_mask);
+  signal(SIGHUP, sighup);
+  signal(SIGTERM, sigterm);
   grabkeys();
   focus(NULL);
 }
@@ -4616,6 +4637,8 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
   run();
   cleanup();
   XCloseDisplay(display);
+  if (restart)
+    execvp(argv[0], argv);
   return EXIT_SUCCESS;
 }
 
